-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 5 -- proceedings instituted or continued with permission`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7736 | 5. A person who is given permission under section 74(1) to institute or continue any legal proceedings must, within 14 days after the date of the order giving such permission or such other period as that order may specify — ( a )
-- src:7737 | file that order, and the process or document by which the legal proceedings are to be instituted or continued; and
-- src:7738 | ( b )
-- src:7739 | serve that order, and that process or document, on every other party to the legal proceedings to be instituted or continued. [S 206/2022 wef 01/04/2022]
@ref O 70 r 5 (src:7736-7739)
GIVEN `the order giving permission specifies another period` IS A MAYBE Period
GIVETH A Period
`o 70 r 5 the period for filing and serving` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the order giving permission specifies another period`
    WHEN JUST other THEN other
    WHEN NOTHING THEN Period WITH
        `period length` IS 14
        `period unit` IS Days
        `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

@ref O 70 r 5 (src:7736-7739)
GIVEN `the person is given permission under section 74(1) to institute or continue legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the order, and the process or document, were filed and served on every other party` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 70 r 5 the order and the process are filed and served within the period` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person is given permission under section 74(1) to institute or continue legal proceedings`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is given permission under section 74(1)"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the date the order, and the process or document, were filed and served on every other party`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not yet filed and served; the period may still be running
         WHEN JUST done THEN
             IF done AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the date of the order giving such permission or such other period as that order may specify"

