-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 70 -- the duties as regulative rules`
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `o 70 party` IS ONE OF
    `o 70 the person that applies for the order`
    `o 70 the person given permission`
    `o 70 the person against whom the order is in force`

DECLARE `o 70 act` IS ONE OF
    `o 70 extract the order and serve it on all other parties`
    `o 70 file the order and the process and serve them`
    `o 70 serve the application and affidavit on the Attorney-General and every other party`

-- src:7727 | 3. —(1) An order under section 74(1) must be in Form 102. (2) An order under section 74(1) must be extracted by the person that applies for the order, and must be served on all other parties to the legal proceedings in respect of which the order was made. [S 206/2022 wef 01/04/2022]
@ref O 70 r 3(2) (src:7727)
`o 70 r 3(2) the duty to extract and serve the order` MEANS
    PARTY `o 70 the person that applies for the order`
    MUST `o 70 extract the order and serve it on all other parties`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 70 the person that applies for the order` BECAUSE "the order under section 74(1) was not extracted and served on all other parties to the legal proceedings in respect of which it was made"

-- src:7729 | 4. —(1) Where an order under section 74(1) is in force against a person, an application by that person for permission under section 74(1) to institute any legal proceedings, or to continue any legal proceedings instituted by that person before the making of that order, and the supporting affidavit for that application, must be served — ( a )
-- src:7730 | on the Attorney-General; and
-- src:7731 | ( b )
-- src:7732 | on every other party to the legal proceedings to be instituted or continued.
@ref O 70 r 4(1) (src:7729-7732)
`o 70 r 4(1) the duty to serve the application for permission` MEANS
    PARTY `o 70 the person against whom the order is in force`
    MUST `o 70 serve the application and affidavit on the Attorney-General and every other party`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 70 the person against whom the order is in force` BECAUSE "the application for permission and the supporting affidavit were not served on the Attorney-General and on every other party"

-- src:7736 | 5. A person who is given permission under section 74(1) to institute or continue any legal proceedings must, within 14 days after the date of the order giving such permission or such other period as that order may specify — ( a )
-- src:7737 | file that order, and the process or document by which the legal proceedings are to be instituted or continued; and
-- src:7738 | ( b )
-- src:7739 | serve that order, and that process or document, on every other party to the legal proceedings to be instituted or continued. [S 206/2022 wef 01/04/2022]
@ref O 70 r 5 (src:7736-7739)
`o 70 r 5 the duty to file and serve the order and the process` MEANS
    PARTY `o 70 the person given permission`
    MUST `o 70 file the order and the process and serve them`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 70 the person given permission` BECAUSE "the order giving permission and the process or document were not filed and served within 14 days after the date of the order"
